From b40bb43f249228fb72454f351675bcca8ebe4446 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ecogamezz <33791269+ecogamezz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:16:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] WowCraft on macOS: the Minecraft link and the drive

wowcraft-link: the SkyCraft shared-memory protocol (version 11 with
WowCraft's additions) and the game's end of it on POSIX shared memory,
tested against the WowCraft mod's own SkyLink in another process.

benilla-app's wowcraft module (WOWCRAFT=1): Minecraft's physics move the
body through a puppet branch in the controller, Minecraft has the keys
and mouse but WoW's own (C, Enter, M, L, B, O), and our view is told to
Minecraft each frame. Verified live against vmangos: a stand-in Minecraft
walked the character 31 yd and the server saved it there.

Built and tested on macOS x86_64 only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
